# Day10

Troubleshoot why mariadb service is not running on DB server and fix it. It is assumed that server is Linux based.

Login into DB server using ssh 
    ssh username@db_hostname
Provide required password for authentication.

Once logged in, check status of the mariadb service using below command

    sudo systemctl status mariadb

In the output we will get relevant information about error while starting service.
	
The error says directory /var/lib/mysql is not empty and because of this mariadb is unable to start.
	
When checked directory /var/lib/ then I could not see directory mysql.

This could be due to possible data corruption or incorrect installation.
	
To overcome this, I tried fresh installation using below command
	
	sudo mariadb-install-db --user=mysql --basedir=/usr --datadir=/var/lib/mysql
	
Post executing above command, I tried to start the mariadb using below command
	
	sudo systemctl start mariadb
	
The database started and it was also enabled, verified using below command
	
	sudo systemctl status mariadb
